       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** 1600 mg four times a day adds up to **6400 mg a day**.\n- The usual maximum single oral dose of ibuprofen is **800 mg**. 1600 mg is twice that.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for adults on prescription is **3200 mg a day**. This order is twice that.\n\nDoses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other NSAID toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**This may be a typo.** Did you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg a day). This may be where the \"1600\" came from.\n- **600 mg four times daily** (2400 mg a day)\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2400 mg a day) or **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg a day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical reason. I'd also strongly suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
